    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "its not just a \"bad phase\" tho. i feel like i have this... structural damage. like a piece of glass that's been crushed into sand. u can't really glue sand back into a vase, u know? people keep telling me to \"keep trying\" but it just feels like they don't get that there's nothing left to try with. its just... fundamentally gone.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you're not just tired—you're grieving a version of yourself you feel you've lost, and that’s a deep kind of pain. Comparing yourself to crushed sand makes sense: some experiences do leave us feeling irreparably changed, and no amount of positivity can undo that reality. But sand isn't \"nothing\"—it can still become something new, like glass again, even if it's not the same vase. You don't have to rebuild what was; you just have to be here, one breath at a time, and let someone sit with you in that truth without trying to fix it. If you can, reach out to a counselor or crisis line—not to be \"fixed,\" but just to have your pain witnessed.",
