      "content": "What you're feeling is real exhaustion, and I'm not going to pretend I can wave it away—that would be dishonest. But when you say \"stop fighting,\" I want you to know that choosing to stay is not about building something grand; it's about giving yourself permission to just exist without a project, without a goal. You don't owe anyone a rebuilt vase—you owe yourself the chance to see what it feels like to be held by others, even when you feel like sand. If the weight is too much to carry alone, please reach out to a crisis line—people will listen without asking you to be anything but honest. You are not a burden for being broken; you are a person who deserves a gentle hand in the dark.",
